.TH CONVEN 1 "August 11, 2026" "Conven" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
conven \- run a focused set of local microservices with remote dependencies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBconven\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
\fBconven help\fR [\fIcommand\fR]
\fBconven\fR [\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
\fBconven\fR [\fB\-v\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conven
is a local microservice launcher.
It starts selected services from a workspace, keeps unselected dependencies
reachable through the configured development infrastructure, materializes
runtime configuration outside the source tree, and records the local session
under
.IR <workspace>/.conven/runtime/current .
.PP
Conven discovers the nearest canonical
.I .conven
workspace from the current directory.
The workspace manifest declares services, environments, connections, runners,
ports, dependencies, and policy-backed configuration adapters.
.PP
For typed local services, startup fails closed unless the selected policy can
prove that remote service registration is disabled or not applicable and that
the service listener is restricted to a loopback address.
Conven does not create a reverse route from the remote cluster to local
services.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize the current workspace.
Conven scans direct-child Git repositories for supported service layouts and
creates
.IR .conven/conven.yaml .
An existing manifest is not overwritten.
.TP
.BR config " [" \-\-global "] [" \-\-list | \-\-unset "] [" key "] [" value "]"
Read, write, list, or remove Conven settings.
Without
.BR \-\-global ,
reads combine global and workspace settings while writes affect only the
workspace configuration.
The valid forms are:
.nf
    conven config [\-\-global] \-\-list
    conven config [\-\-global] key
    conven config [\-\-global] key value
    conven config [\-\-global] \-\-unset key
.fi
.TP
.B policy
Edit, import, or reset the canonical workspace manifest.
Exactly one of
.BR \-\-edit ,
.BR \-\-import ,
or
.B \-\-reset
is required.
.TP
.B plugins
Install, list, remove, or run Python plugins from
.IR ~/.conven/plugins .
Project-specific plugins are not implicitly bundled with Conven.
Use
.BR "\-\-install python-file" ,
.BR \-\-list ,
.BR "\-\-remove name" ,
or
.BR "\-\-run name [plugin-args...]" .
.TP
.B services
List, start, restart, stop, and inspect services in the current workspace.
See
.B SERVICES ACTIONS
below.
.TP
.B doctor
Validate the resolved workspace, selected environment, connection settings,
and static startup configuration without starting services.
.TP
.BR help " [" command "]"
Show the root command overview or detailed help for one command.
For example,
.B conven help services
is equivalent to
.BR "conven services \-\-help" .
.TP
.B version
Print the Conven version.
.SH SERVICES ACTIONS
The action flag must be the first argument after
.BR "conven services" .
.TP
.B \-\-list
List services declared by the workspace manifest.
.TP
.B "\-\-registry [\-\-prune]"
Conservatively update services from direct-child repositories.
Existing non-empty manual declarations take precedence.
With
.BR \-\-prune ,
remove manifest services whose repositories no longer exist.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Show the saved local session, service PID and PGID information, and relevant
shared connection state.
.TP
.B "\-\-dashboard [service...]"
Open the full-screen Dashboard for the current session and optional service
selection.
The equivalent alias is
.BR "services \-\-logs \-\-dashboard [service...]" .
Its fixed banner remains visible while the application retains and scrolls up
to 10,000 lines received by the viewer. The initial replay budget is shared
across selected log sources; subsequent lines are retained in arrival order.
Use the mouse wheel, Up/Down, or PgUp/PgDn to browse, Home or
.B g
for the oldest retained line, and End or
.B G
to resume live follow mode.
Use
.B /
to search,
.BR n / N
to move between matches, and Esc to clear the search.
Press
.B q
or Ctrl-C to detach without stopping services.
This application-level search is independent of terminal search; Command+F can
only inspect the currently rendered Dashboard frame.
If the terminal is unsuitable for the Dashboard, the action fails with guidance
to use
.BR "services \-\-logs \-\-tail" .
.TP
.B "\-\-logs [\-\-tail] [\-\-dashboard] [service...]"
Show logs for the current session.
With
.BR \-\-tail ,
follow new output in a plain continuous stream on the terminal primary screen.
The stream enters native terminal scrollback and can be searched with
Command+F, subject to the terminal profile's scrollback limit.
On attachment, an initial replay budget of up to 10,000 lines is shared across
the selected log sources before following new output.
Use Ctrl-C to detach from the plain stream without stopping services;
.B q
is a Dashboard-only control.
With
.BR \-\-dashboard ,
open the same full-screen viewer as the independent Dashboard action.
If both mode options appear, they are evaluated from left to right and the last
one selects the effective mode.
.TP
.B "\-\-start [options] [service...]"
Start a fresh local service session.
Without service names, open the interactive selector and require confirmation.
After safety and static validation, Conven rebuilds
.IR runtime/current ,
establishes the configured connection, materializes configuration, prepares and
builds services, starts them in dependency order, and performs health checks.
After a successful start, Conven opens the Dashboard automatically when attached
to a usable interactive terminal.
Without such a terminal, start returns and leaves the services running unless
.B \-\-tail
was explicitly requested.
.TP
.B "\-\-restart [options] [service...]"
Restart named services, or detect changed and exited services in the current
session when no names are supplied.
The fixed runtime directory and existing connection are reused; unchanged
service artifacts, configuration, processes, and logs remain untouched.
Restart returns after completing by default; use
.B \-\-tail
to follow selected logs in the plain stream, or all current-session logs when
no service names were supplied.
.TP
.B "\-\-stop [\-\-force] (service...|\-\-all)"
Stop selected services or the entire current workspace session.
Stopping all services releases the workspace connection lease but preserves
.I runtime/current
until the next fresh start.
.TP
.B "\-\-stop\-all [\-\-force]"
Exact shorthand for
.BR "conven services \-\-stop \-\-all" .
.SH START, RESTART, AND DOCTOR OPTIONS
The following options are available to
.B services \-\-start
and, where noted, to restart or
.BR doctor .
Use action-specific
.B \-\-help
for the authoritative option list.
.TP
.BI \-\-env " name"
Select a manifest environment profile.
The default is
.BR dev .
Available to start and doctor.
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Select the
.B dev
profile.
Available to start and doctor.
.TP
.B \-\-test
Select the
.B test
profile.
Available to start and doctor.
.TP
.BI \-\-kubeconfig " file"
Override the Kubernetes configuration path.
Available to start and doctor.
.TP
.BI \-\-context " name"
Override the Kubernetes context.
Available to start and doctor.
.TP
.BI \-\-namespace " name"
Override the Kubernetes namespace used by the connection.
Available to start and doctor.
.TP
.B \-\-tail
Follow aggregated service logs in a plain continuous stream after a successful
start or restart, overriding start's automatic TTY Dashboard.
Also accepted by
.BR "services \-\-logs" .
It is a boolean switch, not a line-count option.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Resolve and validate a start plan without creating or modifying runtime state,
requesting remote configuration, establishing a connection, building, or
starting processes.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-build
Skip service builds.
A fresh start cannot reuse default artifacts inside
.IR runtime/current ;
restart can reuse current artifacts.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-verify
Skip service health checks.
.SH CONFIGURATION AND POLICY
The canonical workspace manifest is
.IR <workspace>/.conven/conven.yaml .
There is no separate policy file.
Policy profiles in the manifest describe framework, configuration source,
service discovery, materialization, routing, and local-isolation rules.
.PP
.B conven policy \-\-edit
publishes a temporary edited copy only after strict validation.
.B conven policy \-\-import
installs an entire local YAML file, backs up the previous manifest, and does not
merge it with repository scan results.
.B conven policy \-\-reset
destructively rebuilds the whole manifest from facts that built-in analyzers can
prove; manual rules must be restored from the backup or declared again.
.PP
Run
.BR "conven doctor" " and " "conven services \-\-start \-\-dry\-run"
after importing or materially changing a policy.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <workspace>/.conven/conven.yaml
Canonical workspace manifest.
.TP
.I <workspace>/.conven/config
Workspace-local settings.
.TP
.I <workspace>/.conven/.gitignore
Workspace-local ignore rules; initialization non-destructively adds the runtime
directory.
.TP
.I <workspace>/.conven/backups
Backups created before manifest import or reset publication.
.TP
.I <workspace>/.conven/runtime
Private workspace runtime root containing the lock and session state.
.TP
.I <workspace>/.conven/runtime/current
Current artifacts, materialized configurations, and service logs.
.TP
.I ~/.conven/config
User-global settings.
.TP
.I ~/.conven/plugins
Installed user plugins.
.TP
.I ~/.conven/state/connections
Cross-workspace shared connection lease metadata.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CONVEN_EDITOR
Editor command used by
.BR "policy \-\-edit" .
Falls back to
.BR VISUAL ,
then
.BR EDITOR ,
then
.BR vi .
.TP
.B CONVEN_KUBECONFIG
Preferred kubeconfig override when no command-line override is supplied.
.TP
.B KTCTL_KUBECONFIG
Compatibility kubeconfig override used after
.BR CONVEN_KUBECONFIG .
.TP
.B KUBECONFIG
Standard Kubernetes fallback.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored terminal output when set.
.TP
.B TERM
When set to
.BR dumb ,
disable color and the interactive log dashboard.
.PP
Conven injects runtime metadata into service, prepare, and build processes
using variables including
.BR CONVEN_WORKSPACE ,
.BR CONVEN_SERVICE ,
.BR CONVEN_ENV ,
.BR CONVEN_STATE_DIR ,
.BR CONVEN_RUN_DIR ,
.BR CONVEN_CONFIG_DIR ,
.BR CONVEN_ARTIFACT ,
and
.BR CONVEN_SELECTED_SERVICES .
Plugins receive the canonical workspace through
.BR CONVEN_WORKSPACE .
.SH SAFETY
For typed services, the verified adapter contract prevents selected services
from being advertised through the configured remote service registry and
limits their listeners to loopback.
It does not isolate business data or messaging.
Local services may still connect to remote databases, Kafka, RPC endpoints, and
other infrastructure, and may write data or consume messages.
.PP
Use
.B \-\-force
only after verifying the saved PID and PGID.
It bypasses normal process identity checks during stop recovery.
.SH NOTES
Service lifecycle actions are flags under the
.B services
command.
Use
.BR "conven services \-\-start" ,
not
.B conven start
or
.BR "conven services start" .
The former top-level
.BR list ,
.BR discover ,
.BR status ,
.BR logs ,
.BR start ,
.BR restart ,
and
.B stop
commands have been removed.
The former
.B \-\-follow
option is now
.BR \-\-tail .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, displayed help, or an explicit interactive cancellation.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, validation, connection, build, process, or runtime failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid syntax, unknown command, unknown action, or unsupported flag.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
conven init
conven help services
conven policy \-\-edit
conven doctor \-\-test \-\-namespace test
conven services \-\-start \-\-dry\-run api service-a
conven services \-\-start \-\-test \-\-namespace test \-\-tail api service-a
conven services \-\-restart
conven services \-\-logs \-\-tail api
conven services \-\-stop\-all
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brew (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR kubectl (1)
